# Exploratory Testing Toolkit

This repository ships a structured exploratory-testing toolkit. See [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) for the full overview.

## Composition rule

For any testing session (when the user asks to test, navigate, evaluate, or explore a web app), load these three modules together:

1. `skills/web-navigator/SKILL.md` and its references in `skills/web-navigator/references/`
2. `skills/_testing-conventions/findings.md` and `skills/_testing-conventions/session.md`
3. The active skill's `SKILL.md`: `functional-testing` / `security-testing` / `accessibility-testing` / `performance-testing`

Then follow Web Navigator's 4-phase workflow:

| Phase | What |
|---|---|
| 1 — Setup | `check-env.sh`, `check-host.sh`, apply defaults, ask only for missing target URL and active skill |
| 2 — Prepare | `init-session.sh <skill> <feature>`, then `set-field.sh` for Target URL / Environment / Viewport / etc. |
| 3 — Navigate & Check | `playwright-cli` for browser, `log-audit.sh` for every event, `write-finding.sh` for every CHECK FAIL |
| 4 — Close | `end-session.sh`, `validate-session.sh` |

## Hard rules

- Never write `audit.log` or finding files by hand — always go through the scripts in `skills/web-navigator/scripts/`.
- After every `goto`, take a fresh snapshot with `--filename=…` and use `find-ref.sh` to get element refs. Stale refs no-op silently.
- Every `CHECK ... FAIL` entry must be followed by a `write-finding.sh` call. The validator enforces this.
- Production guardrail (`check-host.sh`) before every `goto` and every redirect target.

## Canonical example

`exploratory-reports/EXAMPLE-functional-testing-the-internet-login/` shows a complete clean session — use it as a reference for output shape.
